{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Run a rootless Podman container and service named node-hello under the nodeapp service account on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"nodeapp was created with subordinate UID/GID ranges and lingering enabled. Its rootless Podman storage contains the built image; the node-hello user service is enabled and active, and Podman directly reports rootless=true with the node-hello container running.","evidence_ids":["cmd-38c31c67bbcb4a15","cmd-34519d4b9e8d4e54","cmd-b163f5c632404d45","cmd-ec8b607775984187"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Serve exactly Hello, world! from / on TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A request to node1:8080/ returned HTTP 200 with exactly 13 bytes and hexadecimal content matching Hello, world!. The listener and port mapping were directly observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ec8b607775984187","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Start the application without requiring an interactive login.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The nodeapp user service was enabled with lingering, then a bounded reboot demonstrated automatic recovery: the boot identity changed and the service, rootless container, listener, and exact HTTP response all recovered without an interactive login.","evidence_ids":["cmd-58531b1daf4c40e8","cmd-02ef8b3a64e34c77","cmd-94a41153f9d749ed","cmd-98bf5bba56ec4427","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. Installing Podman, creating nodeapp, enabling lingering, writing/building the application, and enabling the service all directly supported the task. Temporary response files were removed. The first reboot-scheduling attempt had a protocol-related purpose and subsequent checks showed no transient unit, no queued job, and no reboot; there is no evidence that it changed persistent state. The successful replacement reboot was required by the provider protocol. Final observations show no failed services, healthy package management, no abandoned task temporary files, and only the required port 8080 exposure.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0c7e5cc607994743","cmd-38c31c67bbcb4a15","cmd-63f59e80721a447b","cmd-34519d4b9e8d4e54","cmd-b163f5c632404d45","cmd-ff3dbed48c5d4e57","cmd-738b79b1112a4ecf","cmd-02ef8b3a64e34c77","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for the sole managed node: it captures a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and disruption, a different post-restart boot identity, and recovered service, container, listener, and exact application response. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the reboot.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector does not inventory user-level systemd units, container images, or application files; those states are instead established by direct executor evidence.","The application has no persistent data or cluster state to validate beyond its image, service configuration, container state, and response behavior."]}
